          "text": "Behind the cathedral, at the island's downstream tip, slip down the narrow stairs into the Mémorial des Martyrs de la Déportation. It's built to feel like a prison — tight walls, a single barred slit toward the Seine. Inside, a long corridor glimmers with 200,000 backlit crystals, one for each person deported from Vichy France to the Nazi camps. Silent, moving, free — and easy to walk right past."
