          "name": "Île Saint-Louis",
          "map": "Pont Saint-Louis Paris",
          "text": "Cross the small Pont Saint-Louis (usually with a busker) onto Paris's quieter island — a planned 17th-century quarter of elegant stone mansions that still feels like a village. Its spine, Rue Saint-Louis-en-l'Île, is lined with little shops and the famous Berthillon ice cream (scooped at many cafés). A good place to slow down."
        },
        {
          "name": "Latin Quarter",
          "map": "Rue de la Huchette Paris",
          "text": "Back on the Left Bank you enter the Latin Quarter — the student district around the Sorbonne since the 1200s, named for the Latin that scholars spoke here until the Revolution. The knot of lanes around Rue de la Huchette is touristy now and full of cheap eats, but the medieval street plan is genuine."
        },
