          "name": "Saint-Séverin",
          "map": "Église Saint-Séverin Paris",
          "text": "Duck into this Flamboyant Gothic church, one of the oldest on the Left Bank. Walk behind the altar to its treasure: a double ambulatory where the vault ribs spiral down into a single central pillar carved to look like a twisting palm tree. The abstract 1960s stained glass in the apse glows in warm color."
        },
        {
          "name": "Shakespeare and Company",
          "map": "Shakespeare and Company Paris",
          "text": "Across the river from Notre-Dame stands the world's most famous English-language bookshop — a cramped warren of rooms where, by tradition, young writers ('Tumbleweeds') have slept among the shelves in exchange for a little work. Opened in 1951, it borrowed the name of Sylvia Beach's 1920s shop that first published Joyce's Ulysses. Head upstairs for the reading room and the resident piano."
        },
