          "name": "Sainte-Chapelle",
          "map": "Sainte-Chapelle Paris",
          "text": "The reason to walk the island. Louis IX (Saint Louis) built it in just seven years — finished 1248 — as a jewel-box for what he believed was Christ's Crown of Thorns. The low ground-floor chapel is the warm-up; climb the tight spiral stairs to the upper chapel and 15 walls of 13th-century stained glass soaring 50 feet, 1,113 scenes running Genesis to Christ (begin at the back-left window, read bottom to top). Go on a bright day. Your Museum Pass covers entry."
